 mode = dualsense
 ```
 
+### Steering wheel games
+
+With `mode = wheel` the game finds the console's steering wheel (a Logitech
+G29, plugged into the PS5 with its mode switch on PS4) the way Windows finds
+one plugged in by USB (Logitech's `046d:c24f`, "G29 Driving Force Racing
+Wheel"): steering, accelerator, brake and clutch, the D-pad and 24 buttons,
+which DirectInput reads as a driving device. The game sees no controller in
+this mode; button lines still add keys, and Cross and the D-pad still answer
+a pop-up. The wheel must be plugged in before the game starts; without one,
+the controller is the game's Xbox controller, as in `mode = xinput`. No force
+feedback yet. See [Steering wheel](WINE_PS5_BUILD.md#steering-wheel).
+
+```ini
+[input]
+mode = wheel
+```
+
